diff --git a/Assets/xml/Text/CIV4GameText_advc.008.xml b/Assets/xml/Text/CIV4GameText_advc.008.xml
index b1dd9395c..3a1815e3c 100644
--- a/Assets/xml/Text/CIV4GameText_advc.008.xml
+++ b/Assets/xml/Text/CIV4GameText_advc.008.xml
@@ -246,10 +246,12 @@
 	
 	<!-- advc.250b: Added mention of the new SPaH option and a clarification
 		 that later-era start and advanced start are separate things.
-		 Overwrites text in Civ4GameText_BTS.xml. -->
+		 Overwrites text in Civ4GameText_BTS.xml.
+		 advc.004g: "Single Player menu" instead of "Single Player game menu"
+		 to avoid any confusion with the in-game "Game Menu". -->
 	<TEXT>
 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_LATE_START_PEDIA</Tag>
-		<English>[H1]Advanced Start[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The Advanced Start system allows players to begin a game of Civilization 4 in a later era, customizing their civilization as though they'd played the game up to their starting year. To play an Advanced Start game, go to the "Custom Game" option under the Single Player game menu. The Advanced Start checkbox is listed under "Game Options." This option is also available in the multiplayer game setup screen. [BOLD]AdvCiv[\BOLD]: Clarification - Games can be configured to start in a later era without enabling Advanced Start; it's a separate mechanism. About the new Start-Points-as-Handicap option, see the AdvCiv manual. If that option is not selected, then Advanced Start works as described here without fundamental changes.  [NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Advanced Start Rules[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]Players will receive a certain amount of Gold which may then be spent on Cities, Buildings, City Population, Culture, Units,  Improvements, Technologies, and Plot Visibility. Certain items, once purchased cannot be removed, so be sure you really want them. These items are: Techs, Cities, Culture, and Visibility. Units and Buildings must be placed in cities. Buildings, Population, and Improvements may all be removed once placed by selecting the item from the Advanced Start menu and then right clicking on the plot where the item you want to remove is located. [PARAGRAPH:1]Leader Traits and Resources which would normally reduce the production time of select buildings or units now provide discounts to such items. For example, an Expansive leader may build [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]Harbors[\LINK] at a discount while a leader with access to the Stone resource may build [LINK=BUILDING_WALLS]Walls[\LINK] at half price. The amount of Gold a player receives depends upon the size of the map, the era in which the player begins their game, and their selected Difficulty Level. The later the era, the larger the map, and the lower the selected handicap, the more Gold the player receives. By starting a Custom Game in either Single or Multiplayer, players can adjust the number of Advanced Start points available for that game.[PARAGRAPH:1]The player may then place items on the map. Players may only place items for which they have the appropriate technologies and resources. By using gold to purchase new techs, more advanced units, buildings, etc. become available. Extended visibility may be purchased to expand a player's usable territory. Improvements can give access to necessary resources. Any gold that is not used during the Advanced Start phase is added to the player's treasury when the game starts. </English>
+		<English>[H1]Advanced Start[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The Advanced Start system allows players to begin a game of Civilization 4 in a later era, customizing their civilization as though they'd played the game up to their starting year. To play an Advanced Start game, go to the "Custom Game" option under the Single Player menu. The Advanced Start checkbox is listed under "Game Options." This option is also available in the multiplayer game setup screen. [BOLD]AdvCiv[\BOLD]: Clarification - Games can be configured to start in a later era without enabling Advanced Start; it's a separate mechanism. About the new Start-Points-as-Handicap option, see the AdvCiv manual. If that option is not selected, then Advanced Start works as described here without fundamental changes.  [NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Advanced Start Rules[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]Players will receive a certain amount of Gold which may then be spent on Cities, Buildings, City Population, Culture, Units,  Improvements, Technologies, and Plot Visibility. Certain items, once purchased cannot be removed, so be sure you really want them. These items are: Techs, Cities, Culture, and Visibility. Units and Buildings must be placed in cities. Buildings, Population, and Improvements may all be removed once placed by selecting the item from the Advanced Start menu and then right clicking on the plot where the item you want to remove is located. [PARAGRAPH:1]Leader Traits and Resources which would normally reduce the production time of select buildings or units now provide discounts to such items. For example, an Expansive leader may build [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]Harbors[\LINK] at a discount while a leader with access to the Stone resource may build [LINK=BUILDING_WALLS]Walls[\LINK] at half price. The amount of Gold a player receives depends upon the size of the map, the era in which the player begins their game, and their selected Difficulty Level. The later the era, the larger the map, and the lower the selected handicap, the more Gold the player receives. By starting a Custom Game in either Single or Multiplayer, players can adjust the number of Advanced Start points available for that game.[PARAGRAPH:1]The player may then place items on the map. Players may only place items for which they have the appropriate technologies and resources. By using gold to purchase new techs, more advanced units, buildings, etc. become available. Extended visibility may be purchased to expand a player's usable territory. Improvements can give access to necessary resources. Any gold that is not used during the Advanced Start phase is added to the player's treasury when the game starts. </English>
 		<French>[H1]D&#233;marrage avanc&#233;[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Le syst&#232;me de d&#233;marrage avanc&#233; vous permet de commencer une partie de Civilization IV &#224; une p&#233;riode tardive, comme si vous aviez jou&#233; au jeu depuis l'ann&#233;e de d&#233;part. Pour faire une partie avec d&#233;marrage avanc&#233;, s&#233;lectionnez l'option "Partie personnalis&#233;e" dans le menu solo. "D&#233;marrage avanc&#233;" se trouve dans "Options de jeu". Cette option &#224; cocher est aussi disponible dans l'&#233;cran de configuration des parties multijoueur.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]R&#232;gles de d&#233;marrage avanc&#233;[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]Vous recevez une certaine quantit&#233; d'or, que vous pouvez d&#233;penser pour acheter des villes, des b&#226;timents, de la population, de la culture, des unit&#233;s, des am&#233;liorations, des technologies et des unit&#233;s ou pour am&#233;liorer votre champ de vision. N'achetez que les &#233;l&#233;ments que vous voulez vraiment, car certains ne peuvent pas &#234;tre supprim&#233;s une fois plac&#233;s. Ces &#233;l&#233;ments sont : les technologies, les villes, la culture et le champ de vision. Les unit&#233;s et les b&#226;timents doivent &#234;tre plac&#233;s dans les villes. Pour supprimer les b&#226;timents, la population et les am&#233;liorations apr&#232;s les avoir plac&#233;s, s&#233;lectionnez-les dans le menu de d&#233;marrage avanc&#233;, puis faites un clic droit sur la case o&#249; se trouve l'&#233;l&#233;ment que vous voulez supprimer. [PARAGRAPH:1]Les ressources et les traits de caract&#232;re des chefs, qui r&#233;duisaient le temps de production de certains b&#226;timents et de certaines unit&#233;s, r&#233;duisent d&#233;sormais leur co&#251;t. Un chef accessible, par exemple, peut construire des [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]Ports[\LINK] pour un prix r&#233;duit, alors qu'un chef ayant acc&#232;s &#224; de la pierre peut construire des [LINK=BUILDING_WALLS]Murailles[\LINK] pour la moiti&#233; de leur prix. La quantit&#233; d'or que vous recevez d&#233;pend de la taille de la carte, de la p&#233;riode &#224; laquelle vous commencez la partie et du niveau de difficult&#233; s&#233;lectionn&#233;. Plus la p&#233;riode de jeu est r&#233;cente, plus la carte est grande et plus le niveau de difficult&#233; est faible, plus vous recevez d'or. En commen&#231;ant une partie personnalis&#233;e en mode solo ou multijoueur, vous pouvez r&#233;gler le nombre de points de d&#233;marrage avanc&#233; disponibles pour la partie.[PARAGRAPH:1]Vous pouvez ensuite placer des &#233;l&#233;ments sur la carte, mais seulement si vous disposez des technologies et des ressources n&#233;cessaires. En utilisant de l'or pour acheter de nouvelles technologies, vous d&#233;bloquerez des unit&#233;s avanc&#233;es, des b&#226;timents, etc. Vous pouvez &#233;tendre votre territoire utilisable en d&#233;pensant de l'or pour am&#233;liorer votre champ de vision. Les am&#233;liorations peuvent donner acc&#232;s aux ressources n&#233;cessaires. Tout l'or que vous n'utilisez pas durant la phase de d&#233;marrage avanc&#233; est ajout&#233; &#224; votre tr&#233;sor au d&#233;but de la partie.</French>
 		<German>[H1]Fortgeschrittener Start[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Mit dem Fortgeschrittenen Start k&#246;nnen Sie ein Civilization 4-Spiel in einem sp&#228;teren Zeitalter beginnen, indem Sie Ihre Zivilisation so konfigurieren, als ob Sie bereits bis zum Startjahr gespielt h&#228;tten. W&#228;hlen Sie dazu im Einzelspieler-Men&#252; die Option "Eigenes Spiel" und hier unter "Spieloptionen" die Option "Fortgeschrittener Start". Im Multiplayer-Men&#252; steht diese Option im Bildschirm "Spiel-Setup" zur Verf&#252;gung.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Regeln f&#252;r den Fortgeschrittenen Start[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]Die beteiligten Spieler erhalten jeweils einen bestimmten Goldbetrag, den sie f&#252;r St&#228;dte, Geb&#228;ude, die Stadtbev&#246;lkerung, die Kultur, Einheiten, Modernisierungen, Technologien und die Gel&#228;ndefeld-Sichtbarkeit verwenden k&#246;nnen. Bestimmte Spielelemente lassen sich nach ihrem Erwerb nicht mehr entfernen, daher sollten Sie sich gut &#252;berlegen, ob Sie sie auch wirklich haben wollen. Hierbei handelt es sich um: Technologien, St&#228;dte, Kultur und Sichtbarkeit. Einheiten und Geb&#228;ude m&#252;ssen dar&#252;ber hinaus in St&#228;dten platziert werden. Geb&#228;ude, Bev&#246;lkerung und Modernisierungen k&#246;nnen nach ihrer Positionierung auf der Karte allerdings auch wieder entfernt werden, indem Sie das gew&#252;nschte Objekt im Men&#252; "Fortgeschrittener Start" ausw&#228;hlen und dann mit der rechten Maustaste auf das Gel&#228;ndefeld klicken, auf dem es sich befindet. [PARAGRAPH:1]Die Merkmale der Staatsoberh&#228;upter und Ressourcen, die normalerweise die Produktionszeiten f&#252;r die gew&#228;hlten Geb&#228;ude oder Einheiten senken, bewirken nun Preisnachl&#228;sse. So ist die Errichtung von [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]H&#228;fen[\LINK] f&#252;r expansiv orientierte Staatsoberh&#228;upter nun beispielsweise mit weniger Kostenaufwand verbunden, und Herrscher, die &#252;ber die Ressource "Stein" verf&#252;gen, k&#246;nnen [LINK=BUILDING_WALLS]Stadtmauern[\LINK] zum halben Preis bauen. Der Goldbetrag, der einem Spieler zugestanden wird, ist von der Gr&#246;&#223;e der Karte, dem Startzeitalter und dem gew&#228;hlten Schwierigkeitsgrad abh&#228;ngig. Dabei gilt: Je fortgeschrittener das Zeitalter, je gr&#246;&#223;er die Karte und je geringer der gew&#228;hlte Schwierigkeitsgrad, desto mehr Gold erh&#228;lt der Spieler. Nach dem Start eines "Eigenen Spiels" im Einzelspieler- oder Multiplayer-Modus k&#246;nnen die Spieler die Anzahl der f&#252;r dieses Spiel verf&#252;gbaren Punkte f&#252;r den Fortgeschrittenen Start festlegen.[PARAGRAPH:1]Danach k&#246;nnen sie Spielelemente auf der Karte platzieren, allerdings nur, wenn die daf&#252;r erforderlichen Technologien und Ressourcen bereitstehen. Wer auf fortschrittlichere Einheiten, Geb&#228;ude etc. zugreifen m&#246;chte, kann neue Technologien hinzukaufen. Auch eine gr&#246;&#223;ere Sichtweite l&#228;sst sich zwecks Erweiterung des nutzbaren Territoriums k&#228;uflich erwerben. Au&#223;erdem erm&#246;glichen Modernisierungen den Zugang zu den ben&#246;tigten Ressourcen. Das Gold, das w&#228;hrend der Startphase nicht verwendet wird, wandert zu Beginn des Spiels in die Schatzkammer des Spielers. </German>
 		<Italian>[H1]Avvio avanzato[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Il sistema di Avvio avanzato permette ai giocatori di iniziare una partita di Civilization 4 in un'epoca pi&#249; avanzata, personalizzando le proprie civilt&#224; come se si fosse giocato fino al momento iniziale della partita. Seleziona la voce Partita personalizzata dal menu Giocatore singolo. Questa opzione &#232; disponibile anche nella schermata di impostazione delle partite multigiocatore.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Regole Avvio avanzato[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]I giocatori ricevono un certo quantitativo di oro che pu&#242; essere speso in citt&#224;, edifici, popolazione, cultura, unit&#224;, miglioramenti, tecnologie e visibilit&#224; delle zone. Una volta acquistati, alcuni beni non possono pi&#249; essere rimossi, quindi prendi le decisioni giuste. Le caratteristiche che non possono essere eliminate sono tecnologie, citt&#224;, cultura; e visibilit&#224;. Unit&#224; ed edfici devono essere collocati nelle citt&#224;. Edifici, popolazione e miglioramenti possono essere eliminati una volta posizionati, selezionandoli del menu di Avvio avanzato e poi cliccando con il pulsante destro sulla casella desiderata. [PARAGRAPH:1]Le caratteristiche dei leader e le risorse che ridurrebbero normalmente i tempi di produzione di unit&#224; ed edifici, ora forniscono sconti sull'acquisto. Per esempio, un leader espansionista pu&#242; costruire [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]Porti[\LINK] scontati, mentre un leader che ha l'accesso alla pietra pu&#242; realizzare le [LINK=BUILDING_WALLS]Mura[\LINK] a met&#224; prezzo. Il quantitativo di oro percepito dai giocatori dipende dalla dimensione della mappa, dall'epoca di partenza e dal livello di difficolt&#224;. I giocatori ricevono pi&#249; oro se l'epoca iniziale &#232; avanzata, se la dimensione della mappa &#232; grande e se il livello di difficolt&#224; &#232; pi&#249; basso. Iniziando una Partita personalizzata, a giocatore singolo o multigiocatore, si pu&#242; regolare il numero di punti disponibili nella partita Avvio avanzato.[PARAGRAPH:1]I giocatori posizionano gli oggetti sulla mappa e solamente se si possiedono le tecnologie o le risorse necessarie. Acquistando con l'oro le tecnologie, diventano disponibili unit&#224; ed edifici avanzati. Acquistando visibilit&#224;, si ha la possibilit&#224; di aumentare il controllo sul territorio. I miglioramenti possono fornire l'accesso alle risorse necessarie. Tutto l'oro che non viene utilizzato durante la fase di Avvio avanzato viene aggiunto al tesoro del giocatore. </Italian>

